Hi <%= @convenor.first_name %>,

<% if @failing_since %>
The daily LMS <%= @sync_name %> for <%= @unit.code %> <%= @unit.name %> has failed every night since <%= @failing_since.strftime('%A %-d %B') %>, so <%= @doubtfire_product_name %> has stopped syncing the unit with the LMS.

This is usually an outage of the LMS or of <%= @doubtfire_product_name %>'s LMS connection rather than a problem with the unit's settings. The last error was: <%= @error_message %>
<% else %>
The daily LMS <%= @sync_name %> for <%= @unit.code %> <%= @unit.name %> failed, so <%= @doubtfire_product_name %> has stopped syncing the unit with the LMS until you review it.

<% if @issues.any? %>
The LMS integration no longer matches the LMS course:
<% @issues.each do |issue| %>
  * <%= [issue[:lms_group_name], issue[:message]].compact_blank.join(': ') %>
<% end %>
<% else %>
The error was: <%= @error_message %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

These settings have been turned off:
<% @turned_off.each do |setting| %>
  * <%= setting %>
<% end %>

<% if @failing_since %>
Once the LMS is working again, run a preview import to check what will change, then turn these settings back on in the unit's LMS tab:
<% else %>
Fix the integration in the unit's LMS tab, then turn these settings back on:
<% end %>
